* A macro whose operand subtracts a parameter, with an equate of constants beside it
* (#Base+2*Width-(\2)), called with a label: the equate kept the expression out of the
* link-time aliases (another symbol of the source) until equates of external names went in,
* after which the call set the alias to the negated label, which as refused.
* fixed: pending
* not r68: r68 makes the operand a negated reference to the label, which rof2elf can't take
* expect size: .text 00000008
Width equ 20
Check macro
 cmpi.w #384+2*Width-(\2),d3
 endm
 psect macro_shape_equ_label,0,0,0,0,0
Here nop
 Check 1,Here
 nop
 ends
